        title: "Daily Practice",
        content: `Let the cross reshape your daily rhythms this week:

1. **Morning surrender prayer.** Each morning, before checking your phone or starting your routine, pray Galatians 2:20 back to God in your own words: "The old me has been crucified. Today, let Christ live through me. I receive this day by faith in the One who loved me and gave Himself for me." Note how this posture affects your first decisions of the day.

2. **Audit your "for whom."** At the end of each day this week, review your major decisions and ask: "Did I make this choice for myself or for Christ?" This is not about guilt but awareness. Record one decision each day that you would make differently if you were fully living "for Him who died and rose."

3. **Embrace a voluntary discomfort.** Paul sought the fellowship of Christ's sufferings. This week, choose one small act of self-denial or service that costs you something \u2014 time, comfort, or reputation. Reflect on what that experience teaches you about the shape of a crucified life.`,
