        sectionType: "anchor",
        title: "Anchor Text",
        content: 'Read the following passages carefully before proceeding:\n\n"Do not quench the Spirit. Do not despise prophecies. Test all things; hold fast what is good." \u2014 1 Thessalonians 5:19-21 (NKJV)\n\n"Beloved, do not believe every spirit, but test the spirits, whether they are of God; because many false prophets have gone out into the world. By this you know the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesses that Jesus Christ has come in the flesh is of God, and every spirit that does not confess that Jesus Christ has come in the flesh is not of God." \u2014 1 John 4:1-3 (NKJV)\n\n"To the law and to the testimony! If they do not speak according to this word, it is because there is no light in them." \u2014 Isaiah 8:20 (NKJV)\n\nAs you read, notice: What attitude does Paul prescribe toward prophetic claims? What specific test does John provide? What standard does Isaiah establish for evaluating any message that claims divine origin?',
