        id: "w4s-21-3-4",
        lessonId: "w4l-21-3",
        sectionType: "practice",
        title: "Daily Practice",
        content: "Put stewardship into action across multiple areas of your life:\n\n1. **Realign one priority.** Reflect on Haggai's challenge: Is there an area where personal comfort has quietly displaced a commitment God has placed on your heart \u2014 volunteering, financial generosity, time with family, care for your health? Identify it and take one corrective step this week.\n\n2. **Practice environmental stewardship.** Choose one tangible action this week that honors the Genesis 2:15 mandate \u2014 reduce waste, care for a shared green space, conserve water or energy, or support a community garden. Let it be a small, sustainable habit rather than a grand gesture.\n\n3. **Give to someone across a boundary.** Following Paul's model in Romans 15, extend material or practical help to someone outside your immediate circle \u2014 a different generation, a different culture, a different socioeconomic group. Let the gift express gratitude for what you have received, not superiority over what they lack.",
