        lessonId: "w4l-22-3",
        sectionType: "anchor",
        title: "Anchor Text",
        content: 'Read the following passages carefully before proceeding:\n\n"Therefore, whether you eat or drink, or whatever you do, do all to the glory of God." \u2014 1 Corinthians 10:31 (NKJV)\n\n"Do not let your adornment be merely outward \u2014 arranging the hair, wearing gold, or putting on fine apparel \u2014 rather let it be the hidden person of the heart, with the incorruptible beauty of a gentle and quiet spirit, which is very precious in the sight of God." \u2014 1 Peter 3:3-4 (NKJV)\n\n"Beloved, I pray that you may prosper in all things and be in health, just as your soul prospers." \u2014 3 John 1:2 (NKJV)\n\nAs you read, notice how these texts address the most ordinary dimensions of life \u2014 eating, drinking, appearance, health. What does it mean that even these mundane areas fall under the umbrella of glorifying God?',
        sortOrder: 1
