        title: "Anchor Text",
        content: `Read the following passages carefully before proceeding:

"Stand fast therefore in the liberty by which Christ has made us free, and do not be entangled again with a yoke of bondage\u2026 For you, brethren, have been called to liberty; only do not use liberty as an opportunity for the flesh, but through love serve one another. For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this: 'You shall love your neighbor as yourself.'" \u2014 Galatians 5:1, 13-14 (NKJV)

"Therefore, if you died with Christ from the basic principles of the world, why, as though living in the world, do you subject yourselves to regulations \u2014 'Do not touch, do not taste, do not handle,' which all concern things which perish with the using \u2014 according to the commandments and doctrines of men? These things indeed have an appearance of wisdom in self-imposed religion, false humility, and neglect of the body, but are of no value against the indulgence of the flesh." \u2014 Colossians 2:20-23 (NKJV)

"Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you pay tithe of mint and anise and cummin, and have neglected the weightier matters of the law: justice and mercy and faith. These you ought to have done, without leaving the others undone\u2026 You are like whitewashed tombs which indeed appear beautiful outwardly, but inside are full of dead men's bones and all uncleanness." \u2014 Matthew 23:23, 27 (NKJV)

As you read, notice the sharp distinction Paul draws between liberty and license, and between genuine holiness and human-made regulations.`,
        sortOrder: 1
