        title: "Drawing Confidence from Christ's Ministry",
        content: `The doctrine of Christ's heavenly ministry is not an abstract theological puzzle; it is a source of profound spiritual confidence. The author of Hebrews writes, "Therefore, brethren, having boldness to enter the Holiest by the blood of Jesus, by a new and living way which He consecrated for us, through the veil, that is, His flesh, and having a High Priest over the house of God, let us draw near with a true heart in full assurance of faith" (Hebrews 10:19-22). The language is remarkable: boldness, full assurance, a new and living way. Access to God's presence is not restricted to a select priestly class; it is opened to every believer through Christ.

John adds another dimension: "If anyone sins, we have an Advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous. And He Himself is the propitiation for our sins" (1 John 2:1-2). The word "advocate" (parakletos) means one who is called alongside to help \u2014 a defender, an intercessor. When guilt accuses us, Christ speaks for us. His defense is not based on our performance but on His sacrifice. Paul presses this to its logical conclusion: "Who shall bring a charge against God's elect? It is God who justifies. Who is he who condemns? It is Christ who died, and furthermore is also risen, who is even at the right hand of God, who also makes intercession for us" (Romans 8:33-34). The entire weight of accusation \u2014 from Satan, from conscience, from the law \u2014 is met by the interceding Christ.`,
