        content: 'Ground your understanding of death and hope in Scripture this week:\n\n1. **Write a four-sentence summary** of what the Bible teaches about the state of the dead, citing at least two passages (e.g., Ecclesiastes 9:5-6, John 11:11-14, Psalm 146:4). Share your summary with a study partner and discuss how this understanding differs from popular cultural assumptions about death.\n\n2. **Read 1 Thessalonians 4:13-18 and 1 Corinthians 15:50-58 together.** Notice how Paul grounds hope not in the moment of death but in the moment of resurrection. Write down one phrase from either passage that you find personally comforting and memorize it this week.\n\n3. **Reach out to someone who is grieving.** Do not offer theological lectures \u2014 simply be present. Listen. Share a meal. If the moment is right, share the hope of the resurrection in your own words: "I believe the day is coming when death will be reversed and we will see our loved ones again." Let the hope be personal, not clinical.',
